  "notes": "Advanced Placement track of the AAS in Registered Nursing, transcribed from the official AIAM School Catalog, Edition 2024.5 (published December 2024, 'WI25' Winter 2025 catalog), 'Program of Study — Registered Nursing — Five 12-week Quarters, 15 months'. This track requires, as an admission condition, 19 quarter credit hours and 269 clock hours of transfer credit from a Board of Nursing approved Practical Nursing program (catalog 'PLEASE NOTE' box); the catalog does not enumerate the transfer-block courses by code. The plan below totals the 91 quarter credit hours taken at AIAM (18.5+18.5+16.5+20.0+17.5 = 91.0, matching the catalog's 'Total Credit Hours Taken at AIAM: 91'); the degree requires 110 quarter credit hours minimum including the 19-credit PN transfer block. BIOL 102B (Anatomy & Physiology II) is listed in external_prereqs: the catalog lists it as prerequisite-or-corequisite for BIOL 103, BIOL 104, BIOL 105 and NRS 204c, and for Advanced Placement students it is satisfied by the PN transfer block rather than taken at AIAM (the same transfer block satisfies the MT 100 / BIOL 102A chain and the NRS 111c / NRS 117B references in the NRS 200/201c/204c descriptions). Quarter 4's unlabeled '0 56 3.5' row is recorded as NRS 203Bc Obstetric Nursing: it is the only other 56-clock-hour / 3.5-credit course in the RN curriculum besides NRS 203A Pediatric Nursing (labeled in Quarter 3), and its catalog prerequisites (Prerequisite: NRS 203A; Prerequisite or Corequisite: NRS 202Bc) match exactly the Quarter 3 -> Quarter 4 placement. Quarter 3's 'Pediatric Nursing' row is recorded as NRS 203A per the course-description header 'NRS 203 A Pediatric Nursing 56 hours/3.5 credits'; Quarter 4's 'Cultural Diversity' row is SOC 200 Cultural Diversity per its description header. NRS 115 and NRS 116c list 'Admission to Advanced Placement Option' (an admission status, not a course) as prerequisite, so their prereq arrays are empty. The catalog also publishes a direct-entry (traditional) 8-quarter / 110-credit program of study, but its quarter tables did not extract with course names intact, so it is not transcribed here. transfer_confidence is 'advisory': AAS workforce nursing program; AIAM publishes no TCCNS/articulation equivalencies, so tccns mirrors the local course code.",
